## 2026-09-23T21:05:00Z session — the SDK's auth.verifyEmail() cannot verify against Neon Auth
curl -X POST "$NEON_AUTH_BASE_URL/verify-email?token=invalid" → HTTP 404
curl -X GET  "$NEON_AUTH_BASE_URL/verify-email?token=invalid" → HTTP 401 {"code":"INVALID_TOKEN"}
@neondatabase/auth 0.5.0-beta server-b0OzGjXl.mjs: verifyEmail: { path: "verify-email", method: "POST" }
- resolved: the verification e-mail links to /verification-email/confirmer, which forwards the token as a GET through the SDK's own /api/auth proxy handler, so Neon's session cookie is set on this origin.
- rule: never call auth.verifyEmail() from @neondatabase/auth 0.5.x (it POSTs; Neon's verify-email is GET-only); go through getAuth().handler().GET with path ["verify-email"].

